  "complexity": 3,
  "title": "fix round 1 for T-1490: strengthen gitutil tests (since count, non-git dir, failed git call), rename-source parity with daemon._dirty_scope_paths, one _resolve_base with timeout, head read once",
  "spec": "Fix round for T-1490 (goal T-1403, B4a), branch cut from task/T-1490 (commit 4753edf implemented gitutil.execute_outcome, head_sha, parse_porcelain_z and the _git_in timeout). The security review T-1502 held it with request_changes. Address exactly its four comments; nothing else.\n\n1. `since` test cannot fail (tests/test_gitutil.py:29). In the scratch repo make at least two commits on the task branch after the merge-base with goal/<parent>. Assert execute_outcome(...) without since reports ahead == 2 and with since=<sha of the first of those two commits> reports ahead == 1. A bug that ignores `since` must fail this test.\n\n2. Missing None cases (tests/test_gitutil.py:34). Add: an existing directory that is not inside any git work tree (a fresh tempdir, not a nonexistent path) returns None; a git call that exits non-zero (patch gitutil._git_in to return a CompletedProcess with returncode=1) returns None. Keep the existing nonexistent-path and TimeoutExpired cases.\n\n3. Rename/copy source parity (orchestrator/gitutil.py:13). daemon._dirty_scope_paths yields both the destination and the source of a rename/copy pair; parse_porcelain_z drops the source. Make parse_porcelain_z yield both paths, exactly like the daemon, so the parity holds for any scope. Extend the parity test so its scope includes the rename source path (old/name.txt) and assert the two sets are still equal. Document in the parse_porcelain_z docstring that a rename contributes both paths because the source path is a deletion.\n\n4. Low: route the merge-base candidate loop through _resolve_base by giving _resolve_base an optional timeout parameter instead of a second copy of the fallback order; make execute_outcome call head_sha instead of re-implementing rev-parse; read HEAD before the status call and read it again after, and if it moved return None (document: concurrent commit, caller retries on the next tick).\n\nDo not rename or weaken existing tests. If a change in gitutil.py is needed for a test to pass, it is in scope; daemon.py is not in scope (the parity test imports daemon._dirty_scope_paths read-only, and gitutil must still not import daemon). Commit first, then run tests/test_gitutil.py in the foreground; never background a command and never run the full gate.",
  "inputs": [],
  "acceptance": [
    "tests/test_gitutil.py::test_execute_outcome_since_counts_only_commits_after_sha: passes: two commits after the merge-base give ahead 2 without since and ahead 1 with since=<first commit sha>",
    "tests/test_gitutil.py::test_execute_outcome_none_for_non_git_dir_and_failed_git_call: passes: an existing non-git tempdir returns None; a patched _git_in returning returncode=1 returns None; nonexistent path and TimeoutExpired still return None",
    "tests/test_gitutil.py::test_parse_porcelain_z_matches_daemon_dirty_scope_paths: passes with the test scope including the rename source path old/name.txt: gitutil.parse_porcelain_z and daemon._dirty_scope_paths give the same path set, and gitutil does not import daemon",
    "tests/test_gitutil.py::test_execute_outcome_reports_ahead_head_and_dirty_split_by_scope: still passes; execute_outcome uses head_sha and returns None when HEAD moves between the two reads (patched)",
    ".claude/hooks/tests-green.sh wt/THIS-TASK exits 0"
  ],
